Licensing status — please read before reusing

This repository is a derivative work. It builds on TUSF's original proposal,
"A draft for a block writing system, designed for Lojban"
(https://gist.github.com/TUSF/d85c3d241c90fede0ea7065ed1107fd5), which does
not carry an explicit license.

Because the upstream work's licensing terms were never stated, this project
is not in a position to assert a license (permissive or otherwise) over the
material it inherits from that proposal — the letter inventory, the four
consonant base-shape families, and the general Hangul-block concept.

What this means in practice:

  - The new material contributed in this draft — the vowel redesign, the
    recursive block-layout rule, the syllabification rule, the lujvo
    stacking rule, the punctuation system, the converter code, and this
    documentation — is offered for reading, discussion, and non-commercial
    experimentation.
  - If you want to redistribute, fork publicly, or build a product on top
    of this work, please first reach out to TUSF (the original author) to
    clarify terms for the inherited material, and treat this repository's
    own additions as available under the same terms you agree with them,
    or under a permissive license (e.g. CC-BY-4.0 or MIT) if TUSF or a
    maintainer later formalizes one.
  - This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by TUSF. If you are
    TUSF and would like different attribution, a specific license applied,
    or this derivative taken down, please say so and it will be honored.

No warranty of any kind is provided. Use at your own risk.
